@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple SysML-style requirements traceability diagram. Four
'                 requirement bubbles traced to one design element and one test
'                 via satisfy/verify/derive/trace dashed edges.
'   usecase:      Teaching the requirement block (stereotyped box with id+text),
'                 the four trace edge stereotypes (derive, satisfy, verify,
'                 trace), and what "coverage" means at a glance.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       systems engineering / requirements
' ============================================================================

title Requirements Traceability - Simple

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' TEACHING NOTES
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' A requirement diagram answers "is every requirement satisfied by design and
' verified by test — and where did each requirement come from?"
'
' The requirement BLOCK: a rectangle stereotyped <<requirement>> with two
' compartments: an Id (e.g. REQ-001) and a Text (the statement). In TheRobotDrafts
' we render this as a stereotyped rectangle; full SysML tools use a special
' requirement shape.
'
' Four dashed-edge stereotypes — all point FROM the thing that depends TO the
' thing depended-on:
'
'   derive    : one requirement is derived/refined from another
'               (stakeholder -> system req). "I got this FROM you."
'   satisfy   : a design element (block/component) satisfies a requirement.
'               "I implement this in hardware/software."
'   verify    : a test case verifies a requirement.
'               "I prove this works."
'   trace     : a generic link to any related artifact (rationale, source doc).
'               "This is relevant to that."
'
' Reading coverage: a requirement with NO incoming satisfy edge is unsatisfied
' (a design gap); with NO incoming verify edge it is unverified (a test gap).
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

' === Requirements (stakeholder + derived system) ===
rectangle "REQ-001\nThe system shall allow\nusers to export a diagram\nas PNG." as R1 <<requirement>>

rectangle "REQ-002\nThe exporter shall render\nat >= 300 DPI." as R2 <<requirement>>
rectangle "REQ-003\nThe exporter shall complete\nwithin 5 seconds." as R3 <<requirement>>

' R2 and R3 are DERIVED from R1 (stakeholder -> system refinement).
R2 ..> R1 : <<derive>>
R3 ..> R1 : <<derive>>

' === Design element that SATISFIES a requirement ===
rectangle "PNG Export\nModule" as PngModule <<component>>

PngModule ..> R2 : <<satisfy>>
PngModule ..> R3 : <<satisfy>>

' === Test case that VERIFIES a requirement ===
rectangle "Test: ExportSpeed" as T1 <<testcase>>
T1 ..> R3 : <<verify>>

' === Generic trace to a source artifact ===
file "Stakeholder\nRequest #42" as Source
R1 ..> Source : <<trace>>

note bottom of R2
  **Coverage at a glance**
  R2: satisfied (by PngModule), NOT verified — test gap.
  R3: satisfied AND verified — fully covered.
  --
  Edges read "I depend on that":
    design  ..> req  : satisfy
    test    ..> req  : verify
    sysReq  ..> stkReq: derive
    any     ..> any  : trace
end note
@enduml
